# SECOND INDEPENDENT REPLICATION of the same stage, same configuration:
#
#   XGBoost             13.5 -> 13.9   (-0.4)   identical to run 1
#   RandomForest         0.2 ->  0.0   (+0.2)   identical to run 1
#   LogisticRegression  53.8 -> 53.8   ( 0.0)   run 1 gave 54.6 -> 53.9
#
# The two tree ensembles reproduce exactly. Logistic regression moves between
# runs, as it does across every refit in this study, because lbfgs terminates
# on the 2,000-iteration limit rather than on convergence.
#
# CONCLUSION. Removing TransactionDT changes the validation-to-test decline by
# at most 0.7 percentage points, and for XGBoost the decline grows slightly
# rather than shrinking. The confound raised in Section 4.7 does not hold:
# extrapolation on the time index does not account for the degradation that
# Section 4.5 attributes to concept drift.
#
# The graph models were not ablated. Retraining alone moves them by up to
# 0.0070 AUPRC (see 09_o5_explainability.log), which is the same order as the
# effect being measured, so the test would be inconclusive.
